{
  "_source": "HCM 7th Edition, Chapter 34 (Interchange Ramp Terminals: Supplemental), Example Problem 2: Parclo A-2Q Interchange (Exhibits 34-17 through 34-29). I-75 at Newberry Avenue, pretimed three-phase signals at both terminals, C = 140 s, PHF = 0.95, D = 800 ft, 11.7% heavy vehicles on the external and internal through movements, 2% grade on the NB and SB ramp approaches, EB/WB left-turn radii 80 ft and 50 ft on every other turn, start-up lost time 3 s and extension of effective green 2 s throughout (total lost time 6 s, Exhibit 34-24). Green intervals reproduce Exhibit 34-23 with both offsets zero: Intersection I phases 0-25 / 30-90 / 95-135 (NEMA 2+5, 2+6, 4+7) and Intersection II phases 0-25 / 30-65 / 70-135 (NEMA 1+6, 3+8, 2+6). Arrival type 4 on the two internal through-and-right groups (Rp = 1.333 in Exhibit 34-25) and 3 everywhere else.",
  "_note_wb_external_green": "The WB external through holds NEMA 6 through both Phase 3 (70-135) and Phase 1 (0-25) of Intersection II, so its green runs uninterrupted across the cycle boundary and is entered as the single wrapping window 70 s + 95 s. Exhibit 34-23 splits it into two windows because that table starts every row at time zero, but Exhibit 34-24 prints G_A = 95 s and g' = 94 s for that movement, which only the uninterrupted reading gives (two 25 + 65 windows would be 90 s and g' = 89 s, and the published c = 2,222 veh/h needs 94). The EB external through is the same construction at Intersection I and Exhibit 34-23 does print it as one 0-90 window.",
  "_deviation_lane_utilization": "lane_utilization_override carries the published Exhibit 34-20 factors (0.7328 EB / 0.6332 WB). Equation 23-17 reproduces the published leftmost-lane shares exactly with the Exhibit 23-24 Parclo A-2Q three-lane a2 of -0.363, v_L = v_E / v_H and v_R = 0 (EB 1/3 - 0.363 x 198/1066 = 0.2659 against a published 0.2660; WB 1/3 - 0.363 x 368/1249 = 0.2264 against 0.2263), but the rightmost-lane shares need a2 = 0.655 where Exhibit 23-24 prints 0.605 (EB 0.4549 implies 0.6548, WB 0.5265 implies 0.6558). Both approaches imply the same unprinted coefficient, so the engine keeps the printed 0.605 and the fixture supplies the published factors, the same treatment Example Problems 1 and 3 already get.",
  "_note_external_left_storage": "Both external left-turn bays are 200 ft, not 500. The Exhibit 34-17 plan view is drawn to no scale and its handwritten bay dimensions are hard to read at any rendering, so the number comes from Exhibit 34-25 instead, which prints the storage length it used as its own row: La = 800 / 200 / 800 ft eastbound and 800 / 200 / 800 ft westbound. The published R_Q row corroborates it, 1.96 for the EB external left and 0.78 for the WB, against 1.960 and 0.781 from the engine on these inputs. Read the bays as 500 ft and the WB R_Q falls to 0.312, which agrees with nothing published. Do not re-open this from the plan view.",
  "_deviation_edtt": "Exhibit 34-29 publishes EDTT of 20.6 s/veh for O-Ds A, D, F, and G, -15.6 for B and C, 37.7 for E and H, and 0 for I and J. The 15.6 s term is the 800-ft interchange spacing at 35 mi/h and the 5 s difference is the Equation 23-50 deceleration/acceleration term on the four O-Ds that use a loop. E and H are the two loop-ramp O-Ds and the chapter text computes them as 1,200 / (1.47 x 25) + 5 = 37.7, a different design speed from the rest of the table, carried here in design_speed_mph. The Facts section states the loop-ramp extra distance as 1,600 ft while the worked EDTT uses 1,200 ft; 1,200 is what reproduces the published column. Equation 23-50's printed 1.47 conversion leaves the 15.6 s term at 15.55, so the engine's EDTT runs 0.05 s/veh short of the published figures throughout.",
